DC universes Titans has provided plenty  of Easter eggs for fans to find there  are callbacks to old classics set-pieces  and iconic comic book locations and a  whole lot more  here are the easter eggs you might have  missed in Titan's season 2 fairly early  in the episode Aqualad we see Arthur  light aka dr. light torturing dr. Jacob  Finley  for starters their conversation  indicates the two have a history I love  this gladiator look reminds me the time  you went Spartacus on professor su after  failing the freshman physics final we  don't hear a lot of specifics but the  gist of it seems to be that Finley has  won respect and fame on dr. lights  shoulders they make a reference to  failed work light did that Finley was  able to improve upon and subsequently  take all the credit for but that's just  the tip of the iceberg regarding the  relationship between these two let's  back up the name Jacob Finley comes  directly from the comics when we first  meet Finley in 1989 secret origins  number 37 he appears as an apparition to  arthur light in a doctor light costume a  flashback unfolds in which we learned  Finley was the original dr. light before  Arthur light took up the name  and unlike Arthur light Finley wanted to  use his abilities for good after Finley  dies Arthur takes his suit and his  powers but continues to be haunted by  Finley's ghost when dr. light tortures  Jacob Finley a blinking you'll miss it  easter egg pays tribute not to a comic  book or another DC inspired TV show or  movie but to one of titans crew when dr.  light lays a copy of a magazine in front  of Finley Finley's faces on the cover  and the story on him was written by one  James uses well James uses isn't a  d-list supervillain or a well-kept comic  book secret he's no ding-dong daddy  in other words instead James Anthony  uses is the set designer for every  episode of titans second season in the  last few years  OSS has also made a name for himself as  a set designer on series like the  expanse and Star Trek Discovery much of  the episode Aqualad revolves around the  doomed garthe trying to woo Donna Troy  in one of his conversations with Donna  Garth teases her with a joke about her  tongue  Twister of a homeland the mascara to the  mascara its mascara yes this is possibly  a reference to a line of makeup that  most fans have probably forgotten about  in 2011 MAC Cosmetics released a Wonder  Woman themed line of makeup products  complete with Wonder Woman artwork by  renowned artist Michael all read the  line included such products as obey me  nail polish Athena's kiss lip gloss and  yes the mascara mascara toward the  beginning of the fifth episode of season  two Garr goes into Rachel's bedroom and  finds a weird oily black substance  flowing out of and around Raven as she  sleeps eventually it cuts gar and later  in the episode Rachel shows fresh cuts  to Cori on her own back from the nightly  events we don't know what the exact  nature of this energy is yet though it  seems obvious it has something to do  with how Trigon altered Rachel's powers  in the season premiere Asgar enters the  room there's a shot of something that  should probably be raising some alarm  bells that we have yet to hear anyone  mentioning it posted on a cork board  above Rachel's desk are a number of  images that wouldn't necessarily be  disturbing if they weren't being drawn  by the daughter of a demon in fact  they're exactly what you'd expect any  given evil demonic possessed kid to draw  before they go fulbright burn on  everyone around them  Rachel's creative side seems to be very  interested in black  abyssal holes which is likely connected  with the darkness continuing to emerge  from Rachel herself fans have been  waiting for the return of Superboy and  Krypto ever since the first season's  finale gave us a post-credits scene  showing the pair busting out of a Cadmus  laboratory they finally got their wish  with the second season sixth episode  Connor after revisiting that post-credit  scene and giving us a corny commercial  for Cadmus Superboy and Krypto escaped  from the lab in the cold open of Connor  and find themselves faced with a skyline  of the famous city of Metropolis  thankfully the show's creative team  don't forget an important detail  metropolis is most well-known landmark  The Daily Planet building the workplace  of Clark Kent the daily planets most  recognizable physical feature is the  massive  ringed globe on top of the building the  Titans crew does a wonderful job with  the detail you wouldn't notice it if you  weren't looking for it but once you do  there's no mistaking what it is after  his escape Connor walks around  metropolis with Krypto taking everything  in and seeming to revel in it at one  point he stops and raises his arms  taking in the Rays of the Sun visibly  overjoyed to be among humanity rather  than locked away in a lab a nearby  street vendor is selling shirts caps and  other metropolis memorabilia including a  black shirt bearing the Superman logo  the park behind the street vendors is  Centennial Park the fictional metropolis  is answer to New York's Central Park in  DC Comics Centennial Park is the home of  the memorial raised to honor Superman  after he dies in battle with the  rampaging villain doomsday it's a  fitting location for Superboy to be as  he experiences his own form of rebirth  everything that he is experiencing is  for the very first time  in Falun mercy graves and our commandos  raid Titans tower recapturing Connor and  crypto seeing garz transformation powers  in action  mercy decides to bring gar along for  good measure the episode ends with gar  in a lounge like prison watching the  1939 classic The Wizard of Oz it turns  out that there's some meaning to the  choice the scene gar is watching brings  the wicked witches flying monkeys into  view and once you see them it's  difficult to not think of the moment  earlier in the episode when Rachel's  powers summoned a winged gargoyle who  hunts down her new friends abusive  father in both this episode and the  following episode there are references  and reminders of Dorothy's trip to Oz  while speaking to the phantom Bruce  Wayne dick refers to death strokes tiny  tin heart a reference to Oz's tin man  who has no heart and considering the  brain surgery forced on gar in that same  episode he could see him singing if I  only had a brain the two Luthor's  mentioned the most in Connor are the  infamous lex luthor and his father  Lionel but we briefly see at least one  more member of the family  Lena Luthor unlike her brother she's  actually smiling in the family portrait  that Conner finds in the Luthor home and  she's looking lovingly at the same man  we know beat Lex after he'd had too much  to drink  Lena Luthor has kind of a crazy history  in DC Comics depending on which comic  book you read and when it was published  Lena Luthor is either Lex Luthor's  sister or she's his daughter  she's risen to prominence more recently  more so on the small screen than in the  comics Katie McGrath plays Lena luthor  in CW's Supergirl series and became a  regular in the third season most episode  of Titans take their titles from the  name of the character who would be the  focus of that particular our season 2  7th episode Bruce Wayne is a departure  in that while Bruce Wayne shows up quite  a bit it isn't really Bruce Wayne when  Dick Grayson's mentor appears to him it  becomes clear that this isn't the real  Wayne but dick Grayson's insecurities  haunting him in the form of his  surrogate father one such scene is when  dick goes to a club looking for  information on Deathstroke and Wayne  appears on stage  in an unexpected turn of events he gives  us a tribute to the late Adam West oh  joy rapture  ian's Glenn's dance is brief but  longtime Batman fans undoubtedly  recognized it as a callback to Adam  West's campy portrayal of Batman from  the 60s in Batman's first episode Batman  finds himself in a disco with the  Riddler's lovely assistant pulling the  trademark moves Glens Bruce Wayne gives  us on titans and Jericho Slade finally  tells his son the truth about who he is  the story is told through a series of  flashbacks all leading up to Jericho  meeting his father alone in the church  to finally get the truth the meeting  doesn't go well  viewers were no doubt expecting to get  some concrete answers from that Meetup  but sharp eared viewers may have gotten  a wealth of info even earlier in the  episode during the episodes first  flashback you might have missed a super  quick mention of a clandestine group  called hive he was part of a special  unit called hive try to relax  [Music]  hive has been a mainstay in DC Comics  since the early 80s when they first  appear in the pages of New Teen Titans  their acronym stood for hierarchy of  international vengeance and  extermination the group has a long  history of animosity with the Teen  Titans including close ties with the  group known as the fearsome five which  includes villains we've already seen on  Titans like shimmer and dr. light season  two's ninth episode atonement opens with  the Titans disbanding leaving guard to  watch over Connor and Titans Tower  the subsequent montage shows gar going  from optimistic and excited to board and  stir-crazy in three days along with  everything else the post-its car leaves  in the kitchen reflect his devolve a  mental state through the helpful  influence of a couple of great songs and  films on the first day he posts fitter  happier more productive a line from  Radiohead's  fitter happier by day two his emotions  are already sagging a bit too any writes  always look on the bright side of life  which is the song that concludes the  classic 1979 religious satire monty  python's life of brian it is a little  strange that Gard chooses this phrase  since the characters singing it aren't  exactly in an enviable position at the  time my day 3 gar is officially  stir-crazy and he lets us know by  calling back to the 1980 thriller The  Shining rather than any affirmations  Garr writes out all work and no play  makes gar a dull boy on multiple  post-its and sticks them up in a row a  post-it tribute to the moment in the  shining when Wendy discovers what her  homicidal husband has really been up to  all winter dick Grayson's time in prison  represents a major turning point for his  character arc thanks in part to three  new cellmates at first it seems like the  three are more than happy with the idea  of killing dick but eventually Grayson  learns his cell mates are deserters from  a corto Maltese cartel in part because  they refuse to kill on the cartels  orders instead of allowing themselves to  be sent back to corto Maltese where  they'll be killed the three plan and  escape during the tenth episode we find  Lewis the youngest of the three  cellmates carving an image on the wall  above his bunk  he eventually tells  this is Alice ooh a guardian spirit of  his home village that protects his  people in spite of dicks warnings Louise  is convinced Alice ool will help him  escape a bird that comes in the night  and saves people yes he's gonna save us  tonight and we'll be free that  conversation is part of the reason dick  decides to help the inmates near the end  of the episode literally coming out of  the night to save them and sure the  carving on the wall doesn't look much  like the costume dick eventually wears  as Nightwing either here or in the  comics but while Titans goes out of its  way to make it clear that this dude is  all about some wings viewers may have  missed the subtle meaning of that  monochromatic wall carving the word  comes from a la 'soul which is Spanish  for blue wing check out one of our  newest videos right here plus even more  looper videos about your favorite shows  are coming soon subscribe to our YouTube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]  you  [Music]
 

